tion to show the updated draft.\n- **Witness.** A red test under real custody with two clients on one store. The paired control submits the new revision and signs.\n\n## Counting finite fulfillment pairs\n- **Architecture.** One pure test enumerates all 16 ordered pairs of fulfill, fail, cancel and expire at target 3, so both steps stay under the target. It compares `lastNumber` with a count tracked in the test, not with the production fold. Each step drives the real validator, judges and drain.\n- **Security.** Test only. The fixture gives each actor every grant, so the test checks the count while the signer guards stay in place. The note says so.\n- **Simplification.** No generator or shrinking library. The README counts (five tests) and file list agree with the test file.\n- **Witness.** The fault control distinguishes: `fulfill → fail` reads 0 against an expected 1 with the fail effect reset, and the pin check is deselected because the control changes the definition bytes. The note states that the native Counting witness was read, not run.\n\n## Security cleanup\n- **Architecture.** Three small changes. The entry-points document now says that distinct /48s can still fill the creation table and that further identities share the bounded overflow window (my non-blocking item 1 on the stack review). The S7 note drops the incoming-power sentence (item 4). The real-bin CLI case runs `new` and `check` in sequence through one `spawnSync` helper and keeps its 30 s deadline (item 3).\n- **Security.** No source change. The document sentence is accurate against the /48 arithmetic.\n- **Simplification.** The removed `execFile` and `allSettled` overlap saves lines and a second spawn environment. The case passed in the gate.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Revision is opt-in.** An application that never passes the revision keeps the old behavior. The dap-foldkit change that adopts it follows after landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha